Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: apps/list.c
Line: 653
Function: collect_keymanagers
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: sk_EVP_KEYMGMT_new() in list_keymanagers() (line 660) is not checked for NULL. If allocation fails, list_keymanagers() passes a NULL stack to EVP_KEYMGMT_do_all_provided(), which then calls collect_keymanagers() with this NULL pointer. collect_keymanagers() calls sk_EVP_KEYMGMT_push(km_stack, km) on the NULL pointer, causing a NULL dereference. list_keymanagers() also later calls sk_EVP_KEYMGMT_sort(km_stack) unconditionally, which can likewise crash.

Source context:
```c
